meta {
  name: Set My Availability
  type: http
  seq: 8
}

patch {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/me/availability
  body: json
  auth: bearer
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{profileAccessToken}}
}

headers {
  Content-Type: application/json
}

body:json {
  {
    "availability": "available"
  }
}

tests {
  test("returns 200 OK", function () {
    expect(res.getStatus()).to.equal(200);
  });

  test("returns the auth-user blob with the new availability", function () {
    const body = res.getBody();
    expect(body.availability).to.equal("available");
    // Same shape as GET /auth/me — the client overwrites its stored copy.
    expect(body).to.have.property("permissions");
    expect(body).to.have.property("avatarUrl");
  });
}

docs {
  # PATCH /me/availability — set own "taking leads" status (PAC-139 §6)

  **Module:** none (`@SkipTenant`, `@SkipBranch`, `@SkipModule`).
  **Permission:** none beyond a valid access token — the route only ever
  touches the caller's own document (`sub` from the JWT). Nobody sets it for
  someone else, and nothing sets it automatically.

  **Body**

  | field        | type                     | rules                              |
  |--------------|--------------------------|------------------------------------|
  | availability | `"available"` \| `"busy"` | required; `null` is a `400`, not a clear |

  `available` = taking new leads (every account's default). `busy` = not
  taking new leads. It says nothing about being logged in. The vocabulary is
  `USER_AVAILABILITIES` in `@sfa/shared`; the Manager view's Team Activity
  table shows it and the Command Center's "assign to" picker (PAC-138) lists
  only `available` people.

  **Response `200`** — the full auth-user blob, exactly as `GET /auth/me`
  returns it (which now carries `availability`), so the sidebar control can
  replace the stored copy in one step.

  **Errors** — `400` value outside the vocabulary, or missing · `401` no/expired
  token or deactivated user.

  > The value in this request is the default, so a collection run leaves the
  > demo producer as it found them.
}
